.TYPE SY:HELLO.TXT
uJ11 / RT-11FB V05.03 - SD software kit 2026-09-26
TYPE SY:README.TXT for utilities, setup and on-disk documentation.
FRAM modules are not changed by this disk. HG setup: TYPE SY:HG.TXT.


.TYPE SY:BASIC.TXT
DEC BASIC-11/RT-11 V2.1 - uJ11 BUILDS

  B81FIJ.SAV   FIS single, exception-stack adapter; with OR without FPP
  B81FIS.SAV   Original FIS single; use with FPP disabled and rebooted
  B81FPU.SAV   FPP single; requires initialized FP11 module
  B81FPD.SAV   FPP double; requires initialized FP11 module

START AND TEST
  RUN SY:B81FIJ
  ... OPTIONAL FUNCTIONS (ALL,NONE,OR INDIVIDUAL)?
  A
  ... READY
  RUN SY:B81TST
  ... CHECKS= 29  ERRORS= 0
  ... CP81 PASS
  BYE

Use the same B81TST.BAS with B81FPU/B81FPD. Under B81FPD only, also
RUN SY:B81DBL to test the extra precision. BYE returns to RT-11.
For an interactive calculation try PRINT 2+2 at READY.

The B81 names are stable filenames retained from the verified builds.
CP81 in test output identifies the test's origin, not the FPGA version.
All four executables are included separately; no BASIC.SAV alias hides
the selected arithmetic implementation.

B81FIJ adds a 26-byte adapter for the extra FEC/FEA words that RT-11
places on the exception stack when it has detected an FPP. It still
executes FIS in microcode. Without FPP the original stack is passed on.
B81FIS + enabled FPP can mis-handle divide-by-zero and other exceptions;
use B81FIJ, or OFF the FPP slot and reboot first (see UJMOD.TXT).

B81TST covers 29 arithmetic/transcendental/language comparisons.
B81DBL checks extra double precision. Their success is not an exhaustive
test of all hardware or arbitrary PEEK/POKE peripheral addresses.


.TYPE SY:CLOCK.TXT
CLOCK 01.01 - RT-11 TIME ON HDSP

  RUN SY:CLOCK        Run CLOCK.SAV in the ordinary background job.
  FRUN SY:CLOCK       Load CLOCK.REL into the RT-11FB foreground job.

FRUN needs the REL file, not SAV. Both are included on this disk.
Foreground CLOCK leaves background available for commands/programs.
After FRUN press Ctrl-B to select the background console.
To stop foreground CLOCK: Ctrl-F, then Q (no Enter), then Ctrl-B.
UNLOAD F releases the foreground job's allocated memory after exit.
For ordinary RUN, Q, q or UART ESC exits; Ctrl-C is handled by RT-11.
RUN SY:CLOCK.REL is also valid, but uses the ordinary background job.

The sixteen-character display shows HH:MM:SS DD/MM and trailing spaces.
CLOCK reads RT-11 .GTIM; it does not synchronize the host by itself.
Use HGTIME first, or set DATE/TIME with the RT-11 commands.
HG is not required while CLOCK runs. The wait uses .TWAIT (100 ms),
allowing the other FB job to execute. Only changed text is redrawn.

HCMS current control is 0x6C (4.0 mA peak instead of 9.3 mA).
This setting and CLOCK are software only. No FPGA changes are needed.
Stop CLOCK before using other panel programs or starting HG transfers.
The retained ODT also owns the display while the CPU is stopped.

Time accuracy follows the calibrated KW11/OSCH on this particular board.
It is not a crystal RTC. Re-sync after reboot, long debugging stops or
when drift matters. TMRATE measures raw system tick rate; see TESTS.TXT.


.TYPE SY:FP11.TXT
FP11.BIN - SOFTWARE DCJ11 FPP IN HALT FRAM

This optional module emulates the J-11 floating-point instruction set.
It is ordinary PDP-11 firmware, not a hardware multiplier/FPU and not
additional FPGA microcode. The filename does not select an FP11-A CPU.
Arithmetic/profile: DCJ11 release 00.12. Package: relocatable format 4.
Install/enable using UJMOD.TXT, then reboot so RT-11 detects the FPP.

FIS remains implemented in microcode and is independent of this module.
F/D arithmetic, conversions, modes/status, exceptions and PSW operands
are described in project docs/fpp.md and docs/fpp-psw.md.
CPU integer accesses to PSW address 177776 are still unsupported;
this module's FP PSW-operand support does not add integer PSW hardware.

Use RUN SY:B81FPU for single-precision BASIC or RUN SY:B81FPD for double.
Use B81FIJ for FIS BASIC when FPP is enabled. Original B81FIS assumes
the old exception stack and should be used only after FPP OFF + reboot.
ON restores a retained FPP without rereading SD, followed by reboot.

ODT command F shows AC0..AC5, FPS, FEC and FEA. Values are raw octal/hex
words; viewing them does not change the floating-point context.
RUN SY:ODTCHK provides a known AC2 pattern and enters installed ODT.
See TESTS.TXT before running FPTST: it intentionally spins for debugging.

No MMU, register banking or memory-mapped integer PSW is added by this
software kit. A successful BASIC test is not complete J-11 certification.


.TYPE SY:HELLO.TXT
uJ11 / RT-11FB V05.03 - SD software kit 2026-09-26
TYPE SY:README.TXT for utilities, setup and on-disk documentation.
FRAM modules are not changed by this disk. HG setup: TYPE SY:HG.TXT.


.TYPE SY:HG.TXT
HG 01.01 / HGTIME - HOST DISK AND RT-11 SYSTEM TIME

HG.SYS talks to the host through the shared FT2232/JTAG GPIO wiring.
STARTF.COM does not access HG. INSTALL requires the HC1200 GPIO CSR.
Select GPIO with JTAG_EN; stop/unplug the JTAG programmer. The host must
run the current hgfsd, built from lsi11-fpga/host/hg in this repository.

HOST (EXAMPLE)
  TZ=Asia/Yerevan hgfsd --directory /path/to/new-share --clock 1000

Without TZ, hgfsd uses the host's local zone. A fresh share imports its
files into .hg-volume.dsk. If that file already exists, it is authoritative:
copying new files beside it does not automatically update the HG volume.

RT-11
  INSTALL HG
  LOAD HG
  DIR HG:
  COPY HG:FILE.EXT SY:FILE.EXT
  RUN SY:HGTIME
  DATE
  TIME
  UNLOAD HG

Then stop the host daemon to release the shared pins before panel use.
Stop CLOCK and other panel programs before active HG transfers. Do not
press panel keys while hgfsd is running. One reader owns the UART.
Wait for each COPY to finish: 15 KiB can take several minutes at 1 kHz.
A host-script timeout does not cancel an in-progress guest transfer.

HGTIME sets BOTH system date and time via the RT-11 .SDTTM request.
It validates reply status, checksum, calendar and ticks before changing
anything. On failure the old RT-11 time remains intact. No periodic sync
occurs; run HGTIME again when needed, after reboot or long ODT stops.
The monitor is 50 Hz; HGTIME also understands a 60-Hz monitor build.
Supported dates for this V5.03 interface: 1972..2035.
Both the updated HG.SYS and updated host daemon are required for TIME.
HG disk transfer does not require the FPP or ODT modules.

After successful sync and releasing HG pins, RUN SY:CLOCK or
FRUN SY:CLOCK displays RT-11 time. See CLOCK.TXT.


.TYPE SY:ODT.TXT
uJ11 ODT - UART AND 16-CHARACTER PANEL DEBUGGER

Install ODT.BIN with UJMOD; normal reboot initializes it. Short RESET
stops USER execution at an instruction boundary. UART prints ODT>.
Long RESET starts a fresh session, clearing breakpoints and view state.
All numbers below are OCTAL unless X selected HEX. No decimal input.

UART COMMANDS
  H                    Help
  R                    All R0..R7 and PSW, without pauses
  R n [value]          Show / edit register (PSW = 10 octal, 8 hex)
  F [n]                All / one FP register, read only
                       AC0..5=0..5, FPS=6, FEC=7, FEA=10 octal
  M addr [count]       Read USER words (default range below)
  B addr [count]       Read USER bytes
  W addr value         Write word with readback
  V addr value         Write byte with readback
  D [addr [count]]     Disassemble, including opcode/extension words
  L / N                Previous / next known instruction in view history
  S [count]            Step into; at most 100 octal steps
  T                    Step over JSR; otherwise one step
  T limit              Different operation: bounded loop of single steps
  C                    Continue saved/edited context
  G addr               Set PC and run
  P [addr]             List / set persistent breakpoint (maximum four)
  Z [addr]             Clear all / one breakpoint
  U addr               Run to one temporary breakpoint
  O / X                Select octal / hexadecimal
  A / A 0 / A 1        Toggle / disable / enable HDSP auto-scroll
  < / >                Manually move the HDSP window
  K m p n e            MEM/PREV/NEXT/ENTER codes (distinct 20..23 octal)
  ESC or Ctrl-C        Cancel input / stop a dump between lines

RAM access is limited to USER 000000..157777; words must be aligned.
Dump/disassembly count limit is 20 octal. No raw HALT/CSR memory editor.
FP dump requires the active FP11 module; its relocated base is discovered.
Disassembly uses the stopped instruction's FPS mode for F/D and I/L.

PANEL LAYOUT
  7     8     9     C     MEM
  4     5     6     D     PREV
  1     2     3     E     NEXT
  0     A     B     F     ENTER

Outside number entry: 8 step in, 9 step over, A registers, B memory,
C disassembly, D set PC/run, E continue, F OCT/HEX. In HEX input 8..F
are digits. Release a step key before pressing it again.
MEM opens/cancels the menu. PREV/NEXT browse entries or adjacent
registers/words/instructions. ENTER edits a register/word, advances a
disassembly/FP view, or confirms input. PREV erases a digit during input.
FP REGISTERS in the menu opens AC0. Only the PANEL waits at each register;
UART R/F prints the whole set. Long lines scroll to the end and back.
Disassembly remembers 32 known boundaries; HISTORY START is not PC-2.
Panel actions/results are also printed on UART.

BREAKPOINTS AND STEPS
Breakpoints replace instructions temporarily with HALT. Use aligned
instruction starts in your own code, 001000..157776, not data/overlays.
Original words are restored at the ODT prompt. If restoration reports
?BP, do not continue until Z successfully restores the affected code.
T without an argument and U run with IRQ enabled. T checks the return
PC and original SP for JSR. Short RESET interrupts that run.
S and T limit defer ordinary IRQ/trace; an IRQ-dependent routine may
not finish under bounded single-stepping. WAIT remains a wait.
Timers/peripherals do not freeze while stopped. Resync time afterward.

Select GPIO and unplug JTAG. UNLOAD HG and stop its host daemon before
using panel keys. For recovery use long RESET followed by UART ESC.


.TYPE SY:PANEL.TXT
HC1200 PANEL DEMONSTRATIONS

  RUN SY:DSPDEM       Cycle display messages.
  RUN SY:KEYDEM       Display KEY: xx (hex), change RGB with each key.
  RUN SY:RGBDEM       Cycle RGB colors and labels.

Use only one display program at a time; stop foreground CLOCK first.
JTAG_EN must select GPIO. Unplug programmer pins, UNLOAD HG and stop
the host daemon before using keys.

These older demo banners say PRESS PANEL ESC. There is no physical
ESC-labelled button on the current 20-key panel. Demo exit tests key
code 0x13 (023 octal), the default ODT ENTER code. Use that key; UART
Ctrl-C can also abort a running RT-11 background demo.
KEYDEM prints other key codes on HDSP, not UART. These are the same
PNLDRV codes used by ODT. Do not infer a new wiring map from old banners.

The demos use the current dimmed PNLDRV (HCMS control word 0x6C).
They do not install FRAM modules. See ODT.TXT for the debugger's separate
panel menu, hotkeys 8..F, per-register browsing and automatic scrolling.


.TYPE SY:README.TXT
uJ11 SD SOFTWARE KIT - 2026-09-26

RT-11FB V05.03, HC1200, 128 KiB FRAM, no MMU.
UART: 115200 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit, no flow control.
This is a raw RK07 image starting at SD sector 0, not a FAT file.
Write the decompressed image to the WHOLE SDHC/SDXC card on the host.
The project guide docs/sd-image.md explains writing and verification.

Type commands at the RT-11 dot prompt. Do not type the dot itself.
Use SY: explicitly if you have changed the default DK: device.
TYPE SY:filename.TXT reads a manual. Ctrl-S pauses; Ctrl-Q resumes.

DOCUMENTS AND PROGRAMS
  UJMOD.TXT   UJMOD.SAV: install, enable, disable and list FRAM modules
  UJBOOT.TXT  UJBOOT.SAV: software reboot through the resident bootstrap
  ODT.TXT     ODT.BIN: UART/panel debugger, steps and breakpoints
  FP11.TXT    FP11.BIN: optional software DCJ11 FPP
              SDBOOT.BIN: optional replaceable SD bootstrap (UJMOD.TXT)
  HG.TXT      HG.SYS and HGTIME.SAV: host disk and system time sync
  CLOCK.TXT   CLOCK.SAV / CLOCK.REL: HDSP clock, including FB foreground
  PANEL.TXT   DSPDEM.SAV, KEYDEM.SAV, RGBDEM.SAV: panel demonstrations
  BASIC.TXT   B81FIJ, B81FIS, B81FPU, B81FPD and two BASIC test programs
  TESTS.TXT   TMRATE.SAV, ODTCHK.SAV, FPTST.SAV: diagnostics

FIRST START
  The disk boots without optional FRAM modules. FIS is in microcode.
  Existing valid AUTO modules in FRAM remain active after normal reset.
  Copying BIN files to SD does not install/update them in HALT FRAM.
  RUN SY:UJMOD, then STATUS, shows the existing eight slots.
  Read UJMOD.TXT before changing an existing installation.
  The startup file does not install FRAM modules or start the clock.
  It disables SL and prints this kit's short welcome.

QUICK START
  RUN SY:B81FIJ  - FIS BASIC, usable both with and without FPP.
                  Answer A to the optional-functions question.
                  Type BYE at READY to return to RT-11.
  RUN SY:HGTIME  - sync RT-11 time after LOAD HG and starting the host.
  FRUN SY:CLOCK  - HDSP clock with a separate background console.
                  Ctrl-B selects the background console.

PANEL AND RECOVERY
  Select GPIO with JTAG_EN and unplug the programmer from shared pins.
  Stop the HG host daemon and UNLOAD HG before using panel keys.
  Short RESET enters installed/initialized ODT; C continues execution.
  Long RESET (about two seconds) restarts and checks retained modules.
  UART ESC immediately after long RESET bypasses all optional modules.
  The built-in fallback still needs a readable bootable SD card.

The standard DEC tools from the source distribution remain on the disk:
DIR, PIP, DUP, EDIT, MACRO, LINK, LIBR, HELP and others.
The boot monitor is FB. Included SJ/XM distribution files do not imply
XM support: the current uJ11 FPGA has no enabled MMU.
Text manuals use ASCII/CRLF for the standard RT-11 terminal.


.TYPE SY:TESTS.TXT
uJ11 SOFTWARE DIAGNOSTICS

TMRATE.SAV - SYSTEM TICK SAMPLING
  RUN SY:TMRATE
Prints CFG and 121 raw high/low .GTIM pairs, about 50 ticks apart.
At 50 Hz the run takes about two minutes. UART Q/q/ESC exits early.
The host must timestamp arrivals with a monotonic clock to calculate
frequency; raw numbers alone are not a wall-clock measurement.
No date/time, divisor or FPGA setting is changed. Do not synchronize
time during this measurement. The current board divisor is 596037.
Host automation: tools/hardware_clock_rate.py (project source tree).

ODTCHK.SAV - INTERACTIVE FP DEBUGGER CHECK
Requires installed/initialized ODT and FP11, with RT-11 freshly booted
after their activation. Stop CLOCK and release HG pins first.
  RUN SY:ODTCHK
The program loads AC2, sets double mode and HALTs into ODT automatically.
  ODT> F 2
Expected raw words: 040200 012345 067012 034567 (octal).
  ODT> F 6
FPS has D mode set; other FPS bits may be retained from earlier software.
  ODT> C
The guest prints !ODTCHK-I-RETURNED TO RT11 and exits.
Without ODT/FPP this diagnostic is not a safe stand-alone smoke test.

FPTST.SAV - AUTOMATED ODT/FPP REGRESSION FIXTURE
Not a run-to-completion utility. It raises IPL to 7, executes a sequence
of FPP instructions and intentionally loops for ODT inspection.
The source and symbol maps drive tools/run_rt11.py, which single-steps
and later redirects execution to FINISH for additional assertions.
Do not expect Ctrl-C at its loop: ordinary interrupts are masked.
Short RESET enters installed ODT; long RESET reboots for recovery.
For ordinary user validation prefer BASIC tests and ODTCHK above.

B81TST.BAS / B81DBL.BAS - see BASIC.TXT.
DSPDEM / KEYDEM / RGBDEM - see PANEL.TXT.
UJMOD STATUS shows retained-module checksums/initialization status;
the old OK bit after an ESC bypass is not proof of active services.


.TYPE SY:UJBOOT.TXT
UJBOOT 01.00 - SOFTWARE RESTART

  RUN SY:UJBOOT

Restores the production bootstrap/resident code, enters HALT startup,
validates and initializes enabled modules, then boots RT-11 from SD.
Use after installing modules or ON/OFF configuration changes.
No FPGA programming or physical RESET is needed for this normal path.

Finish file transfers first. Stop/unload foreground jobs and stop HG
activity. Restart ends the current RT-11 session, including all jobs.
ODT breakpoints/context are reinitialized; module code stays in FRAM.
Set/synchronize date and time again after a restart.

UJBOOT requires a working RT-11, CPU and resident entry. For a hung CPU,
bad module initializer or broken software bootstrap use the physical
long RESET plus UART ESC fallback instead. That bypasses optional
modules and still requires a valid SD card.

This utility does not change the FPGA image or program its FLASH.


.TYPE SY:UJMOD.TXT
UJMOD 04.00 - RETAINED HALT FRAM MODULES

RUN SY:UJMOD starts the loader. At UJMOD> enter ONE command.
It returns to RT-11 after that command; run it again for the next one.

  STATUS       List slots 0..7: BASE LENGTH CHECKSUM STATUS, all octal.
  NAME         Load SY:NAME.BIN at its preferred address.
  NAME AUTO    Relocate to a free aligned range in the module's pool.
  OFFn         Disable slot n at the next normal boot; keep its bytes.
  ONn          Check retained checksum and re-enable slot n without SD.
  DELn         Remove the slot/allocation; does not erase the old bytes.
  EXIT         Return without changes.

BIN files on this disk use format 4 / ABI3 with DEC relocation records.
The loader reserves code AND BSS/stack and checks overlap and readback.
Names have 1..6 letters/digits, with no extension or device prefix.
SDBOOT uses the small bootstrap pool. ODT and FP11 use the main pool.
Same BASE replaces a slot. AUTO allocates a NEW slot/range: it is not
an in-place update by module name. STATUS first; do not create duplicate
ODT or FPP services. To replace a relocated module, DEL its old slot,
then install the new NAME AUTO and reboot.

EXAMPLE FOR AN EMPTY TABLE ONLY
  RUN SY:UJMOD
  UJMOD> ODT
  RUN SY:UJMOD
  UJMOD> SDBOOT
  RUN SY:UJMOD
  UJMOD> FP11 AUTO
  RUN SY:UJBOOT
  ... wait for RT-11FB ...
  RUN SY:UJMOD
  UJMOD> STATUS

FP11 is optional; omit its installation for FIS-only operation.
SDBOOT is replaceable software; the built-in ROM remains a fallback.
In an empty table this sequence places ODT at 010000, SDBOOT at 006000
and FP11 at 042710. Slot numbers and addresses are not module types.

STATUS (OCTAL)
  140403  Installed, AUTO enabled, cold initialization not yet confirmed
  140407  Successfully initialized in the last normal boot
  140413  Validation/initialization failure
  140401  Retained, AUTO disabled
  140402  Incomplete installation; bootstrap skips it
  000000  Empty
LENGTH counts immutable words, not bytes or the complete allocation.
After ESC boot an old OK bit is not proof of current activation.

Installation/OFF/DEL disable live HALT services. Finish all module
changes, then RUN SY:UJBOOT or long RESET without ESC. Do not run FPP
software between a configuration change and reboot. ON also requires
reboot to apply. RT-11 detects FPP availability at boot time.

Example: STATUS identifies FPP as slot 2. OFF2 then reboot disables it;
ON2 then reboot restores it from FRAM with no need to reload FP11.BIN.
ODT and SDBOOT are retained independently.

Recovery: long RESET, immediately send UART ESC, wait for RT-11,
then use UJMOD to disable/remove/replace the faulty module. An initializer
can have a valid checksum and still hang: the physical recovery path
does not depend on it. There is no automatic module watchdog.


